\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Repair gain at $b{=}10$ against the unbiased baseline's learning term. The qualitative regularity (weak baseline, larger gain) holds within MNIST and Fashion separately, but a quantitative law fails: ConvADNet-Fashion has $24.7$ points of $\ell $-headroom and no significant gain. Headroom is necessary-looking, not sufficient.}}{9}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:headroom}{{3}{9}{Repair gain at $b{=}10$ against the unbiased baseline's learning term. The qualitative regularity (weak baseline, larger gain) holds within MNIST and Fashion separately, but a quantitative law fails: ConvADNet-Fashion has $24.7$ points of $\ell $-headroom and no significant gain. Headroom is necessary-looking, not sufficient}{figure.3}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces What the bias buys and what it charges ($T{=}10$, $b{=}10$, paired means). The bare MLP sits in the gain--gain quadrant; every strong-feature cell falls in the learning-vs-retention trade quadrant, with final accuracy significantly negative in $3/4$.}}{10}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:tradeoff}{{4}{10}{What the bias buys and what it charges ($T{=}10$, $b{=}10$, paired means). The bare MLP sits in the gain--gain quadrant; every strong-feature cell falls in the learning-vs-retention trade quadrant, with final accuracy significantly negative in $3/4$}{figure.4}{}}
